---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
---

<Layout>
  <section class="container design-hero">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">DESIGN & EXPERIENCE</p>
      <h1>
        Good software
        <br />
        <em>makes space.</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="intro-copy">
        Space to understand. Space to decide. Space to do the work that deserves
        your attention. A considered interface starts by asking what can become
        simpler.
      </p>
      <a class="arrow-link" href="#principles">
        A closer look at the details <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="design-composition">
      <p class="mini-label">FORM WITH A PURPOSE / CIVOLYN DESIGN STUDY</p>
      <div
        class="type-specimen"
        role="img"
        aria-label="Manrope and Instrument Serif type specimen"
      >
        Aa<em>a</em>
      </div>
      <div class="specimen-bottom">
        <span>
          A clear voice.
          <br />A little human character.
        </span>
        <div
          class="design-colors"
          role="img"
          aria-label="Ivory, near black, cobalt, mist and sage palette"
        >
          <span style="background:#f7f6f2"></span>
          <span style="background:#111318"></span>
          <span style="background:#2048ec"></span>
          <span style="background:#dce4fa"></span>
          <span style="background:#b6c7b7"></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="note-strip">
    <div class="container">
      <span>
        Manrope for clarity. Instrument Serif for a moment of expression. All
        fonts are served locally.
      </span>
      <span>AN ORIGINAL VISUAL SYSTEM</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section class="section" id="principles">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">SMALL CHOICES. A DIFFERENT FEELING.</p>
          <h2>
            Give attention
            <br />
            <em>somewhere useful to go.</em>
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          Calm is not the absence of detail. It is knowing which detail belongs
          in front of you, and which can wait until you need it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="principles-grid">
        <article>
          <span class="number">01 / LEGIBILITY</span>
          <h3>Readable before remarkable.</h3>
          <p>
            Clear type, useful line lengths and a deliberate hierarchy make the
            page easier to scan. Labels explain an action before a person has to
            guess.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="number">02 / COGNITIVE LOAD</span>
          <h3>One decision at a time.</h3>
          <p>
            Show a useful starting point, then make the supporting detail
            available. In Knowledge, a result opens to reveal its snippet and
            source without taking the reader away.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="number">03 / HUMAN CONTROL</span>
          <h3>An action should mean something.</h3>
          <p>
            Flow tells you when the example is waiting for review. Buttons
            describe the next step, and reset provides a way back to the
            beginning.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="number">04 / INCLUSION</span>
          <h3>More than one way to understand.</h3>
          <p>
            Use a keyboard to navigate, read Signal’s data table, or reduce
            motion through device settings. An interface should not demand a
            single way of seeing or moving.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section feature-demo-section">
    <div class="container split-section">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">FEEL THE DIFFERENCE</p>
        <h2>
          Make the next step obvious.
          <br />
          <em>Then let people choose.</em>
        </h2>
        <p>
          A small control can communicate a lot: what you can do, what will
          happen and whether it has a consequence. This selector changes a local
          destination. It does not submit a form.
        </p>
        <a class="arrow-link" href="/journal/#human-judgment">
          Read about designing for judgment <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="design-demo" data-preview-picker>
        <h3>Your starting point.</h3>
        <p>Choose a concept to explore. No account needed.</p>
        <label for="design-product">Product preview</label>
        <select id="design-product">
          <option value="flow">Flow</option>
          <option value="knowledge">Knowledge</option>
          <option value="signal">Signal</option>
        </select>
        <a
          class="button button-blue"
          href="/products/flow/#preview"
          data-preview-link
          style="margin-top:20px"
        >
          Open Flow preview ↗
        </a>
        <p class="demo-note">
          Fictional concept · The next page contains local sample interactions.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container split-section">
      <div class="design-composition" aria-hidden="true">
        <p class="mini-label">MOTION, IN SERVICE OF MEANING</p>
        <div class="type-specimen">
          <em>→</em>
        </div>
        <div class="specimen-bottom">
          <span>Acknowledge a choice.</span>
          <span>Respect a preference.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">PURPOSEFUL MOTION</p>
        <h2>
          A little movement.
          <br />
          <em>A clear reason.</em>
        </h2>
        <p>
          A subtle entrance can establish rhythm. A state change can confirm an
          action. Neither should stand between a person and the content.
        </p>
        <p>
          This website follows reduced-motion preferences. There are no autoplay
          videos, timed workflow steps or moving charts to keep up with. The
          previews progress at your pace.
        </p>
        <a class="arrow-link" href="/support/">
          Read about using the previews <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CTA title="Thoughtful design is better experienced." />
</Layout>
